  "notes": "RELATED WORDS:\n- {遺失物|いしつぶつ} - lost property (formal/legal term)\n- {忘|わす}れ{物|もの} - forgotten item (left behind, not dropped)\n- {拾|ひろ}い{物|もの} - found item\n\nUSAGE:\n{落|お}とし{物|もの} specifically refers to items accidentally dropped, while {忘|わす}れ{物|もの} refers to items left behind or forgotten.\n\nLOST AND FOUND:\nIn Japan, lost items have a high return rate. Items can be reported or collected at police boxes ({交番|こうばん}) or dedicated {落|お}とし{物|もの}センター at train stations.",
